    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass (2/2, the full suite). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the Owner resource, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `ownerSegment` read-only property to the `Owner` schema as a string enum with the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field and `OwnerSegmentEnum` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Region.java`** \u2014 Added `isKnownRegion(String)`, returning `true` only for NSW/VIC/QLD (backed by the existing region-postcode table).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the domain method `getOwnerSegment()`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - AREA = `METRO` when the owner's locality (`Region.regionOfCustomerCode(customerCode)`) is a known region, else `REGIONAL`.\n\n4. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `@AfterMapping` hook that copies `owner.getOwnerSegment()` onto the DTO, matching the existing pattern used for `ageBand`, `locality`, etc.\n\nThe AREA logic reuses `locality` (the region component of the `customerCode`) as the single source of truth \u2014 the same value the existing `locality` field exposes \u2014 so a known city like Sydney (\u2192 `NSW`) yields `METRO` and an unknown city yields `REGIONAL`, consistent with both the spec and the acceptance tests.",
